 ### [Second Order Pre-Integrated Volume Rendering](3388-second-order-pre-integrated-volume-rendering.md)
-Second Order Pre-Integrated Volume Rendering approximates the scalar field using a second-order Lagrange polynomial (quadratic) defined by three equispaced samples. It sets itself apart from First Order Integration by capturing high-frequency details in transfer functions more accurately, reducing the discrepancy between the trilinearly interpolated volume and its piecewise polynomial approximation. Choose this method when the scalar field has significant curvature and higher visual fidelity is required, accepting the cost of a larger lookup table (indexed by three samples). [Second Order Pre-Integrated Volume Rendering](3388-second-order-pre-integrated-volume-rendering.md)
