 ## Background
-Originated from the need to improve rendering quality in direct volume ray casting by addressing the limitations of Riemann sums [S1, unofficial]. The concept of pre-integration was introduced by Engel in 2001 [S2, unofficial]. The method corresponds to the trapezoid rule in numerical integration [S3]. It has been implemented on specialized hardware like the UVIZARD FPGA system (1997) and volumePRO (1999) [S2, unofficial]. Analytic integration for linear variations was first presented by Williams and Max [S4, book].
